    "summary": "Tight second set, stellar Truckin' jam and soaring China Doll",
    "blurb": "The show shines in the second set with a monster Truckin' > Playing In The Band sequence that even teases Here Comes Sunshine. Highlights include a jaw‑dropping Box of Rain vocal, soaring China Doll and volcanic Sunshine Daydream. Jerry’s guitar is rich and fluid while Phil lays down superb bass on Eyes Of The World.",
    "review": "June 9 1973 at RFK Stadium captures the Dead in top form, especially in the second set where they weave a massive Truckin' into Playing In The Band jam that even slips in a Here Comes Sunshine tease. The band rides that energy through a soaring China Doll and a volcanic Sunshine Daydream finale, while Phil’s vocal on Box of Rain has been called jaw‑dropping. Jerry’s playing is smooth and richly textured; his smoky lead on Playing In The Band and the “parallel‑universe” improvisations during breaks add an extra layer of intrigue despite a brief lyric stumble on Half‑Step. Though the first set is more routine, standout moments like Eyes Of The World showcase Phil’s superb bass work and the crisp drum sound that drives the entire performance.",
